Implement LTX-2.3 base model import

Every .ltx2_3 arm of ModelImporter was a fatalError. This adds the inspect()
detection arm and fills the seven switch arms with the wiring LoRAImporter
already uses, plus the prefix-strip loop, the bare-named connector register
writes that UNetFixedEncoder reads back, a 5746-tensor write check, and an
inferModelSpecification arm matching the built-in zoo entry. The four
aggregate_embed mappings are written as BF16 because the text feature
extractor runs BF16 at inference and ccv_nnc_tensor_read cannot convert 16F
to 16BF.

It also fixes a bug in the LTX2.swift mappers. The q and k RMSNorm gain
vectors must be row-interleaved like the to_q and to_k projections they
scale, to match the NNC cmul rotary pair layout. All fourteen were mapped
plain. LoRAs never carry norm gains, so LoRA import never hit it.
Un-interleaved gains produce video that is spatially fine, temporally
frozen, and washed out.
